{
 "_doc": "Orders for Tripo's API (tools/models/tripo.py, run by .github/workflows/models.yml when this file changes on main; needs the secret TRIPO_API_KEY). Key — the model's name (content/art/models/<name>.glb); a model already there is not ordered again unless \"redo\": true. image — the picture to make it from; faces — the generator's face limit; for — what it replaces on the map (see models.json); front — degrees that turn its front to the street; rig — skeleton type (biped, quadruped, hexapod, octopod, avian, serpentine, aquatic); rig_task — a rig already made (only the animations are ordered); animations — the API's preset names (biped: preset:idle, walk, run, jump, slash, shoot, hurt, fall and ~100 preset:biped:*; other rigs — tested 12.10: only their own walk, preset:quadruped:walk, preset:octopod:walk, preset:hexapod:walk, preset:serpentine:march, preset:aquatic:march; idle, slash, hurt, fall fail for them, the game moves them itself). Prices (12.10.2026): model with HD texture ~40 credits, rig 25, an animation 10; 100 credits = $1. complete — the picture is a portrait: first the whole figure is drawn from it (image-to-image, template character_completion; prompt by the rig or complete_prompt). size — the creature's longest horizontal side in metres, height — a standing figure's height; people — a regex of the map's people names dressed in this model.",
